hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-2 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-2 = cons "Avik Jain" (cons "" (cons "Start with the kernel, because the word knows what it is before we do. *Kernel* is Old English *cyrnel*, a little corn, the seed inside the husk. Every device running the hyperactive kernel is every device carrying the seed, the way every cell carries the genome. The operating system was always meant to be a seed; computing just forgot to plant it." (cons "" (cons "What the seed does is reduce active pairs. In Lafont's nets the cells are called agents, from *agere*, to drive. Two agents meet at their principal ports, and the meeting is an interaction: driving between. Nothing computes alone. So the machine at the bottom of the stack is already the thing in the headline, Hyperactive Interaction, before any human touches a screen." (cons "" (cons "*Interaction* has a twin that nobody pairs with it: *intelligence*. *Intelligere* is *inter* + *legere*, to gather between, to read between, to choose between. *Legere* is the root of *lecture* and *collect* and *elect*, and its Greek cousin *legein* gives *logos* and *logic*. So interaction is driving between and intelligence is gathering between. Superintelligence is gathering between, beyond measure; hyperinteractivity is driving between, beyond measure. The two words joined in the name of the work are one structure seen from two sides: the act and the reading of the act." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "What is gathered is data, and *data* is the plural of *datum*, " (cons "given" (cons ". Data is what is given. *Information* is *in-formare*, to give shape to something, to put form into it. So the 1970 erasure has an exact description in the words: it kept the given and threw away the form. Data without meaning is the given without its shape, and every industry that reconstructs meaning is putting the form back." nil)))) (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "The person who receives what is given has their own word in Jewish mysticism. *Kabbalah* is " (cons "receiving" (cons ": what is handed down and taken up. The Latin for handing down is *tradere*, which gives *tradition*, and also, with a turn, *traitor*: one who hands over. Giving, receiving and handing over are the three motions of any transmission. Knowledge transmission in hyperactivity is all three: the given (data), the shape (information), and the receiving (the reader who takes it up whole)." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "Receiving whole is what a symbol was built for. A Greek *symbolon* was a token broken in two. Each party kept a half, and identity was proven when the halves fitted back together: *syn* + *ballein*, thrown together. A symbol is a proof of identity by fit. That is content addressing and it is the active pair: two halves meet, and if they fit, they are the same transaction. The opposite word is *diabolos*, *dia* + *ballein*, thrown across, thrown apart: the slanderer, the one who splits what belongs together. A symbolic nervous system is, in the words, a body of cords whose parts prove their identity by fitting together." (cons "" (cons "The cords are literal. Greek *neuron* meant sinew, tendon, bowstring. A nervous system is a system of strings under tension. *Tension* comes from *tendere*, to stretch, the same root as *intention* and *extension*. So the nervous system is made of the same stuff, in the words, as intention and as the tool's extension of a person. Defining HCI as the extension of consciousness by tools describes a nerve growing outward: the cane is a sinew the blind person stretches into the ground." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "*System* is *syn* + *histanai*, to stand together. *Compositional* is *com* + *ponere*, to put together. So " (cons "compositional symbolic nervous systems" (cons " reads, root by root: things put together, thrown together so they fit, made of stretched cords, standing together. Every word in that formulation is a word of joining." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "The boundary where joined things meet is where hyperactivity puts logic: logical compatibility at every expressed boundary. *Compatible* is *com* + *pati*, to suffer together. *Pati* is the Latin of *passion* and *patient*, and its Greek counterpart *pathos* is inside *empathy*. Compatibility, at the root, is co-suffering. So the phrase says there is co-suffering at every boundary that gets expressed: wherever two systems meet, each takes the other's state into itself. A type check at a boundary is a formal empathy: one side admits what the other is, exactly as it is." (cons "" (cons "That is why social conformity and logic belong to one inquiry. Where normative cognition resolves to group baselines and suppresses rational inference whenever a bounded group defends its boundary, compatibility fails at the root: one side refuses to receive the other's reality. In the type system, such a boundary fails to check. A system logically compatible at every expressed boundary has no mechanism for pretending the other side is other than it is." (cons "" nil)))))))))))))))))))))
